module proximalLigationDetection
module cellTypeDetection
module proteinComplexDetection
module macrophageSignalDetection

manifest PBMCs
manifest Jurkat_Cells
manifest Raji_Cells
manifest ProxSeqProbes_A
manifest ProxSeqProbes_B
manifest BSA_PBS
manifest FcBlocker_TruStainFcX
manifest RNaseInhibitor
manifest LigationBuffer_HEPES
manifest ConnectorOligomer_IDT
manifest T4_Ligase_NEB
manifest PropidiumIodide
manifest SmartSeq2_LysisBuffer
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant_2pct
manifest PBS_1pct_BSA
manifest DropSeq_Beads
manifest LPS_100ngmL
manifest PAM_40ngmL
manifest PFA_4pct
manifest TruStainFcX
manifest ProxSeqProbes_TLR_Panel
manifest LigationBuffer_TLR

// ============================================================
// Quantification of Extracellular Proteins, Protein Complexes
// and mRNAs in Single Cells by Proximity Sequencing
// Vistain, Van Phan, Keisham, Jordi, Chen, Reddy & Tay
// Nature Methods, Vol. 19, December 2022, pp. 1578-1589
// DOI: 10.1038/s41592-022-01684-z
//
// Prox-seq combines proximity ligation assay (PLA) with
// single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) to simultaneously
// measure extracellular proteins, protein complexes (up to
// n^2 pairwise), and mRNAs from thousands of single cells.
//
// Three experimental arms are encoded in sequence:
//
// ARM 1: Jurkat/Raji T-cell/B-cell mixture validation
//   (Drop-seq-based Prox-seq; 11-protein panel)
//   - Fc block, probe incubation, ligation, Drop-seq encapsulation
//   - PLA products and cDNA processed into sequencing libraries
//   - QC gate on PLA cell-type signal
//
// ARM 2: PBMC 38-marker panel (plate-based Prox-seq)
//   - 741 potential pairwise protein complexes measurable
//   - Identifies CD9-CD8 complex on naive CD8+ T cells
//   - 10x Genomics arm for simultaneous mRNA + PLA readout
//   - QC gate on protein complex detection signal
//
// ARM 3: Primary human macrophage TLR signalling panel
//   - 15 NF-kB pathway surface protein targets (225 PLA products)
//   - Stimulation: LPS (TLR4), PAM (TLR2), or both; 5 min / 2 h / 12 h
//   - PFA fixation preserves receptor interactions pre-staining
//   - QC gate on macrophage signalling signal (TLR2-TLR2 complex)
//
// PROBE DESIGN NOTES:
//   Each protein target has a Probe A and Probe B (both DNA-
//   conjugated antibodies). Oligomers are ligated via a universal
//   connector region (119 bp PLA product). Only ligated products
//   (requiring both Probe A and Probe B in proximity) are captured
//   downstream by poly-A tail on the oligomer.
//   Probe concentration: 5 nM total per pair (2.5 nM A + 2.5 nM B).
//
// LIGATION CONDITIONS:
//   50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP, 9.5 nM connector
//   oligomer (IDT), 130 U/mL T4 ligase (NEB); 37 C for 30 min
//   (3 h for plate-based Jurkat/Raji).
//
// SEQUENCING READ DEPTH:
//   >= 10,000 reads/cell recommended for PLA products (Extended
//   Data Fig. 9). Plate-based (Smart-seq2): 75 bp read 1.
//   Drop-seq: 20 bp read 1 / 85 bp read 2 / 8 bp i7 index.
//
// DURATION TOKENS (lilott8/BioScript compiler):
//   Only `s` (seconds) and `m` (minutes) are valid.
//   All time values converted accordingly.
//   2 h  = 120m  |  12 h = 720m  |  37 C probe incubation = 30m
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                -- entry: T/B cell validation (Drop-seq)
//   BB2  cellTypePass        -- cellTypeSignal > 0: PLA cell types
//                              detected; dispose; continue to BB4
//   BB3  cellTypeFail        -- cellTypeSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB4  cellTypeJoin        -- join: PBMC arm (plate-based) begins
//   BB5  complexPass         -- complexSignal > 0: protein complexes
//                              detected (incl. CD9-CD8); dispose
//   BB6  complexFail         -- complexSignal <= 0: no complexes; drain
//   BB7  complexJoin         -- join: macrophage TLR arm begins
//   BB8  macrophagePass      -- macrophageSignal > 0: TLR complexes
//                              detected; dispose all stimulated samples
//   BB9  macrophageFail      -- macrophageSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup        -- terminal: dispose QC signals; end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 1: Prepare Jurkat and Raji cell mixture.
//   150,000 Jurkat (T cells) + 150,000 Raji (B cells) counted,
//   spun 500g/3 min, washed once with 1% BSA/PBS, spun again.
//   Combined and plated in 96-well U-bottom plates.
//   Fixed with 4 mM DSP (dithiobis-sulfosuccinimidyl propionate)
//   in PBS at 37 C for 30 min to preserve surface architecture.
//   `heat` models DSP cross-linking incubation (37 C, 30 min).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

jurkatCells     = dispense 1 units of Jurkat_Cells
rajiCells       = dispense 1 units of Raji_Cells
cellMixture     = mix jurkatCells with rajiCells for 5s

// DSP cross-linking fixation to preserve surface proteins.
heat cellMixture at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 2: Wash and resuspend in probe binding buffer.
//   1% BSA/PBS wash (x1). Resuspend in 90 uL probe binding
//   buffer: PBS + 0.1% BSA + 0.1 mg/mL sonicated salmon
//   sperm DNA (competitor) + 6.7 nM each isotype control.
//   Probe binding buffer suppresses nonspecific antibody
//   binding (confirmed minimal in Extended Data Fig. 5).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

probeBuf        = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
probePanelA     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_A
probePanelB     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_B

// Combine probe pairs into single incubation mix.
// Each pair at 5 nM total (2.5 nM probe A + 2.5 nM probe B).
probesMixed     = mix probePanelA with probePanelB for 5s
probingMix      = mix cellMixture with probesMixed for 5s

// Probe incubation: 37 C for 60 min (= 60m).
heat probingMix at 37c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 3: Wash (x2) then ligate PLA products.
//   Two washes with 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS (500g, 5 min each).
//   Resuspend in 300 uL ligation solution:
//     50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP,
//     9.5 nM connector oligomer (IDT), 130 U/mL T4 ligase.
//   Ligate at 37 C for 3 h (= 180m) with rotation.
//   PI (propidium iodide) added 30 min before end to identify
//   dead cells; live (PI-negative) cells sorted into plates.
//   NOTE: ligation requires both probe A and probe B in
//   proximity; unligated probes discarded during library prep.
//   >90% probes found ligated (Extended Data Fig. 4b).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

washBuf         = dispense 1 units of BSA_PBS
washedCells     = mix probingMix with washBuf for 5s

ligBuf          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer_HEPES
connector       = dispense 1 units of ConnectorOligomer_IDT
t4Ligase        = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase_NEB

ligSolution     = mix ligBuf with connector for 5s
ligSolution2    = mix ligSolution with t4Ligase for 5s
ligatedProduct  = mix washedCells with ligSolution2 for 5s

// 3 h (180 min) ligation at 37 C with rotation.
heat ligatedProduct at 37c for 180m

// Add PI 30 min before end to mark dead cells.
piStain         = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide
piMix           = mix ligatedProduct with piStain for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 4: Drop-seq encapsulation and library prep.
//   Live (PI-negative) cells co-encapsulated with barcoded
//   beads (ChemGenes Macosko-2011-10(V+)) in ~1 nL droplets
//   using HFE7500 + 2% surfactant as the oil phase.
//   Droplets broken; beads subjected to reverse transcription,
//   exonuclease digestion, whole-transcriptome amplification.
//   PLA products (poly-A tail) and cDNA captured together.
//   Processed into separate PLA and cDNA sequencing libraries.
//   `mix` abstracts droplet co-encapsulation on the DMF device.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase        = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant_2pct
dropSeqBeads    = dispense 1 units of DropSeq_Beads

encapsulated    = mix piMix with dropSeqBeads for 5s
dropsEquenced   = mix encapsulated with oilPhase for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 1 - STEP 5: PLA cell-type QC detection.
//   proximalLigationDetection module abstracts alignment of
//   PLA product reads (custom Java program; github tay-lab/
//   Prox-seq). PLA products read out by sequencing (NextSeq
//   Mid-output kit v2.5; 20 bp read 1 / 85 bp read 2).
//   Expected: PD1-CD3 and CD3-CD3 enriched in Jurkat cluster;
//   ICAM1-HLADR and HLADR-HLADR enriched in Raji cluster.
//   cellTypeDetection abstracts the t-SNE / PCA clustering
//   step confirming cell-type segregation (Fig. 1e-j).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellTypeSignal  = detect cellTypeDetection on dropsEquenced for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Cell-type PLA QC gate
// Pass (BB2): cellTypeSignal > 0 -> Jurkat and Raji clusters
//             correctly identified by PLA products; dispose.
// Fail (BB3): cellTypeSignal <= 0 -> no cell-type separation
//             in PLA space; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (cellTypeJoin).
// ============================================================

if (cellTypeSignal > 0) {
    dispose dropsEquenced
} else {
    drain dropsEquenced
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: cellTypeJoin
// Dispose cell-type QC signal. Control falls into PBMC
// 38-marker plate-based Prox-seq arm (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose cellTypeSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 1: Prepare PBMCs.
//   1 million rested PBMCs collected, all centrifugation at
//   300g/3 min. Resuspend in 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS; pellet.
//   Resuspend in Fc blocker: 95 uL 1% BSA/PBS + 5 uL
//   TruStain FcX (BioLegend); incubate 5 min RT.
//   All buffers supplemented with 1:1000 RNase inhibitor (NEB).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcCells       = dispense 1 units of PBMCs
fcBlock         = dispense 1 units of FcBlocker_TruStainFcX
rnaseInh        = dispense 1 units of RNaseInhibitor

blockedPBMCs    = mix pbmcCells with fcBlock for 5m
blockedRNase    = mix blockedPBMCs with rnaseInh for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 2: 38-marker probe incubation (PBMC panel).
//   Panel targeting 38 immune cell markers (primary focus: T
//   cell markers; Supplementary Table 3). Measures up to 741
//   unique protein complexes. Antibody cocktail divided into
//   3 serial portions due to volume; each portion incubated
//   37 C for 15 min before adding the next. Total ~45 min.
//   `mix` steps model the three sequential incubation portions.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcProbesA     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_A
pbmcProbesB     = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_B

pbmcProbesMix   = mix pbmcProbesA with pbmcProbesB for 5s

// Portion 1 (15 min, 37 C).
pbmcPortion1    = mix blockedRNase with pbmcProbesMix for 5s
heat pbmcPortion1 at 37c for 15m

// Portion 2 (15 min, 37 C).
pbmcPortion2    = mix pbmcPortion1 with pbmcProbesMix for 5s
heat pbmcPortion2 at 37c for 15m

// Portion 3 (15 min, 37 C).
pbmcPortion3    = mix pbmcPortion2 with pbmcProbesMix for 5s
heat pbmcPortion3 at 37c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 3: Wash (x3) and ligate.
//   Three washes with 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS (300g, 3 min each).
//   Resuspend in ligation solution (same formulation as ARM 1).
//   Ligate 37 C for 30 min (= 30m).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcWash1       = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
pbmcWash2       = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
pbmcWash3       = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA

pbmcWashed1     = mix pbmcPortion3 with pbmcWash1 for 5s
pbmcWashed2     = mix pbmcWashed1 with pbmcWash2 for 5s
pbmcWashed3     = mix pbmcWashed2 with pbmcWash3 for 5s

pbmcLigBuf      = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer_HEPES
pbmcConnector   = dispense 1 units of ConnectorOligomer_IDT
pbmcLigase      = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase_NEB

pbmcLigSol      = mix pbmcLigBuf with pbmcConnector for 5s
pbmcLigSol2     = mix pbmcLigSol with pbmcLigase for 5s
pbmcLigated     = mix pbmcWashed3 with pbmcLigSol2 for 5s

// 30 min ligation at 37 C.
heat pbmcLigated at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 4: Plate-based library prep (Smart-seq2).
//   PI stain added (1 ug/mL final); live PI-negative cells
//   sorted into 96-well plates (1 cell/well) containing 4 uL
//   Smart-seq2 lysis buffer (0.1% Triton X-100, 1 U/uL RNase
//   inhibitor, 2.5 mM dNTPs, 2.5 uM oligodTVN, 2.5 uM
//   oligodTGT). Non-PFA cells stored -80 C until processing.
//   Plates thawed on ice; incubated 72 C/3 min before library
//   prep. 2-4 uL/well used for PLA product pre-amplification,
//   followed by PCR to attach cell indexes and sequencing
//   adaptor. NextSeq Mid-output kit v2.5 (75 bp read 1).
//   `mix` abstracts Smart-seq2 lysis and library capture.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbmcPI          = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide
pbmcLysisBuffer = dispense 1 units of SmartSeq2_LysisBuffer

pbmcPIStained   = mix pbmcLigated with pbmcPI for 5s
pbmcLibrary     = mix pbmcPIStained with pbmcLysisBuffer for 5s

// Lysis/RT pre-step at 72 C for 3 min.
heat pbmcLibrary at 72c for 3m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 2 - STEP 5: Protein complex QC detection.
//   proteinComplexDetection module abstracts the Protein Complex
//   Estimation Algorithm (iterative quadratic solver; Fig. 2a).
//   Algorithm computes expected random PLA count per complex,
//   subtracts background, identifies statistically significant
//   complexes (one-sided t-test, Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted
//   p < 0.05). 37 protein complexes expected from 10x arm
//   (Supplementary Table 4); CD9-CD8 on naive CD8+ T cells
//   is the key novel finding (Fig. 3f, Fig. 4f).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

complexSignal   = detect proteinComplexDetection on pbmcLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Protein complex QC gate
// Pass (BB5): complexSignal > 0 -> protein complexes (incl.
//             CD9-CD8 on naive CD8+ T cells) detected; dispose.
// Fail (BB6): complexSignal <= 0 -> no significant complexes
//             above random ligation background; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (complexJoin).
// ============================================================

if (complexSignal > 0) {
    dispose pbmcLibrary
} else {
    drain pbmcLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: complexJoin
// Dispose complex QC signal. Control falls into macrophage
// TLR signalling arm (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose complexSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 1: Primary macrophage culture and stimulation.
//   Thawed primary human macrophages (STEMCELL Technologies)
//   plated in 10 wells of a non-tissue-culture 24-well plate.
//   Rested overnight in RPMI + 10% FBS at 37 C.
//   Stimulation: 300g/3 min spin then incubate 5 min / 2 h /
//   12 h with 100 ng/mL LPS (TLR4 agonist), 40 ng/mL Pam2CSK4
//   (TLR2 agonist), or both, in RPMI + 10% FBS.
//   Untreated cells serve as control (10 conditions total:
//   3 ligands x 3 time points + 1 control).
//
//   This BioScript file encodes the 5-minute stimulation arm
//   for LPS, PAM, and both simultaneously -- the time point
//   at which PLA products peak (Fig. 5e). Separate branches
//   share the same fixation and staining procedure.
//
//   NOTE ON FIXATION: Cells are fixed with 4% PFA (15 min RT)
//   AFTER stimulation to preserve receptor interactions at the
//   moment of signalling. The antibody cocktail is applied
//   POST-FIXATION. `heat` at 37 C for 5 min models the
//   stimulation; 25 C for 15 min models PFA fixation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macrophageCells = dispense 1 units of PBMCs
lpsStimulus     = dispense 1 units of LPS_100ngmL
pamStimulus     = dispense 1 units of PAM_40ngmL

// Combined LPS + PAM stimulation (both arm).
stimulusMix     = mix lpsStimulus with pamStimulus for 5s
stimulatedMacro = mix macrophageCells with stimulusMix for 5s

// 5-minute stimulation at 37 C.
heat stimulatedMacro at 37c for 5m

// PFA fixation (4% PFA, room temperature 25 C, 15 min)
// to lock receptor interactions at the stimulation endpoint.
pfaSolution     = dispense 1 units of PFA_4pct
fixedMacro      = mix stimulatedMacro with pfaSolution for 5s
heat fixedMacro at 25c for 15m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 2: Fc block and 15-marker TLR probe incubation.
//   Resuspend fixed cells in 95 uL 1% BSA/PBS + 5 uL TruStain
//   FcX (5 min RT). Resuspend in 54 uL 5 nM Prox-seq probes
//   (15-protein NF-kB panel: CD14, CD36, IL-1R, IL-6Ra, IL-8Rb,
//   IL-10R, LBP, MD2, MMP15, MMP16, TGFBR1, TLR1, TLR2, TLR4,
//   TLR6; Supplementary Table 5). Measures up to 225 protein
//   dimers. Incubate 30 min at 37 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macroFcBlock    = dispense 1 units of TruStainFcX
macroBlocked    = mix fixedMacro with macroFcBlock for 5m

tlrProbesA      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_TLR_Panel
tlrProbesB      = dispense 1 units of ProxSeqProbes_TLR_Panel

tlrProbeMix     = mix tlrProbesA with tlrProbesB for 5s
macroProbed     = mix macroBlocked with tlrProbeMix for 5s

// 30 min probe incubation at 37 C.
heat macroProbed at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 3: Wash (x3) and ligate TLR PLA products.
//   Three washes with 1 mL 1% BSA/PBS (300g, 3 min each).
//   Resuspend in ligation solution and incubate 37 C for 30 min.
//   Fixed cells use modified Smart-seq2 lysis buffer (0.1%
//   Triton X-100, 1000 U/mL RNase inhibitor, 20 U/mL proteinase
//   K, 2.5 mM dNTPs, 2.5 uM oligodTVN, 2.5 uM oligodTGT in
//   TE buffer) sorted into 96-well plates.
//   Plates incubated 56 C / 1 h then 95 C / 10 min before
//   storage at -80 C. Library prep same as ARM 2.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macroWash1      = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
macroWash2      = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA
macroWash3      = dispense 1 units of PBS_1pct_BSA

macroWashed1    = mix macroProbed with macroWash1 for 5s
macroWashed2    = mix macroWashed1 with macroWash2 for 5s
macroWashed3    = mix macroWashed2 with macroWash3 for 5s

tlrLigBuf       = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer_TLR
tlrConnector    = dispense 1 units of ConnectorOligomer_IDT
tlrLigase       = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase_NEB

tlrLigSol       = mix tlrLigBuf with tlrConnector for 5s
tlrLigSol2      = mix tlrLigSol with tlrLigase for 5s
macroLigated    = mix macroWashed3 with tlrLigSol2 for 5s

// 30 min ligation at 37 C.
heat macroLigated at 37c for 30m

// Fixed-cell plate sorting protocol:
// Sorted into plates; 56 C for 60 min then 95 C for 10 min.
macroLysisBuffer = dispense 1 units of SmartSeq2_LysisBuffer
macroPlated     = mix macroLigated with macroLysisBuffer for 5s

// 56 C / 60 min proteinase K digestion step.
heat macroPlated at 56c for 60m

// 95 C / 10 min to inactivate proteinase K.
heat macroPlated at 95c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM 3 - STEP 4: Macrophage TLR signalling QC detection.
//   macrophageSignalDetection module abstracts the logistic
//   regression classifier trained on PLA product levels at
//   the 2-h time point (AUC = 0.82 +/- 0.08; Fig. 6a/b).
//   Key classifier feature: TLR2-TLR2 PLA product (highest
//   logistic regression coefficient for LPS-like response;
//   Fig. 6b). The module also captures the CD36 co-receptor
//   rearrangement observable at 5 min post-LPS (Fig. 6c/d/e).
//   Additive integration of LPS and PAM signals confirmed
//   (non-synergistic; Fig. 5e/f).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macrophageSignal = detect macrophageSignalDetection on macroPlated for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Macrophage TLR signalling QC gate
// Pass (BB8): macrophageSignal > 0 -> TLR2-TLR2 and CD36
//             complexes detected; LPS/PAM-like response
//             classified; dispose stimulated samples.
// Fail (BB9): macrophageSignal <= 0 -> no receptor complex
//             signal above baseline; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (macrophageSignal > 0) {
    dispose macroPlated
} else {
    drain macroPlated
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose macrophage signalling QC signal.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose macrophageSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
